{"title":"Career Roadmap · ADR Case Manager","role":"ADR Case Manager","summary":"An ADR Case Manager manages the administrative, procedural, documentation and coordination aspects of arbitration, mediation, conciliation and other dispute-resolution proceedings.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Alternative Dispute Resolution / Arbitration & Mediation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An ADR Case Manager manages the administrative, procedural, documentation and coordination aspects of arbitration, mediation, conciliation and other dispute-resolution proceedings."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is particularly relevant in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arbitration institutions"},{"text":"Mediation centres"},{"text":"Law firms"},{"text":"Corporate legal departments"},{"text":"Dispute-resolution chambers"},{"text":"Arbitration service providers"},{"text":"Construction/infrastructure disputes"},{"text":"Commercial dispute-resolution practices"},{"text":"International arbitration organisations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"An ADR Case Manager is generally not the arbitrator or mediator. The case manager supports the process by ensuring that filings, communications, deadlines, hearings, documents, fees and procedural requirements are properly coordinated."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated LL.B","ADR / Arbitration Specialisation","ADR / Arbitration Internship","Case Management Executive / ADR Coordinator","ADR Case Manager","Senior ADR Case Manager","Arbitration / Mediation Case Management Lead","ADR Institution Manager / Dispute Resolution Professional"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative law-firm pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Student","Dispute Resolution Intern","Arbitration Paralegal / Legal Executive","Arbitration Case Manager","Senior Arbitration Professional","Dispute Resolution Manager"]}]},{"heading":"What Does an ADR Case Manager Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The case manager acts as the process and coordination hub of a dispute."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Receive and register cases"},{"text":"Maintain case files"},{"text":"Coordinate with parties"},{"text":"Communicate with arbitrators/mediators"},{"text":"Track procedural deadlines"},{"text":"Coordinate hearings"},{"text":"Manage submissions"},{"text":"Maintain document repositories"},{"text":"Prepare procedural calendars"},{"text":"Coordinate virtual hearings"},{"text":"Track fees and administrative requirements"},{"text":"Issue procedural communications where authorised"},{"text":"Maintain confidentiality"},{"text":"Coordinate experts, interpreters and transcription services"},{"text":"Support tribunal appointments"},{"text":"Maintain case statistics"},{"text":"Prepare administrative reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Simplified Model"},{"type":"p","text":"Claimant"},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"├──────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ │"},{"type":"p","text":"ADR Institution │"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ │"},{"type":"p","text":"ADR Case Manager │"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ │"},{"type":"p","text":"Arbitrator / Mediator"},{"type":"p","text":"↑ │"},{"type":"flow","items":["└──────────────┘","Respondent"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact administrative responsibilities depend on the institution, rules and type of proceeding."}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year UG Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Legal Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal methods"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Constitutional law"},{"text":"Torts"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Legal writing"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Business fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ADR Introduction"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Mediation"},{"text":"Conciliation"},{"text":"Arbitration"},{"text":"Litigation"},{"text":"Adjudication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the differences between:"},{"type":"table","header":["Process","Basic Nature"],"rows":[[{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Parties negotiate directly"}],[{"text":"Mediation"},{"text":"Neutral facilitates settlement"}],[{"text":"Conciliation"},{"text":"Neutral assists parties toward resolution"}],[{"text":"Arbitration"},{"text":"Tribunal/arbitrator determines dispute"}],[{"text":"Litigation"},{"text":"Court adjudicates dispute"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Commercial & Procedural Law"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Civil Procedure"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Company Law"},{"text":"Commercial Law"},{"text":"Property Law"},{"text":"Corporate transactions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ADR Focus"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arbitration agreements"},{"text":"Arbitration clauses"},{"text":"Jurisdiction"},{"text":"Appointment of arbitrators"},{"text":"Interim measures"},{"text":"Procedural orders"},{"text":"Evidence in arbitration"},{"text":"Enforcement of awards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a commercial contract and identify:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Dispute Clause","Negotiation","Mediation / Conciliation","Arbitration","Tribunal","Hearings","Evidence","Award","Enforcement / Challenge"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Arbitration & Mediation Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should develop serious ADR expertise."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arbitration law"},{"text":"Mediation law and practice"},{"text":"Commercial arbitration"},{"text":"International arbitration"},{"text":"Institutional arbitration"},{"text":"Ad hoc arbitration"},{"text":"Arbitration procedure"},{"text":"Arbitration agreements"},{"text":"Jurisdictional issues"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Interim measures"},{"text":"Arbitral awards"},{"text":"Enforcement"},{"text":"Settlement agreements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Indian Context"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996"},{"text":"Mediation Act, 2023"},{"text":"Commercial Courts framework"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Civil procedure"},{"text":"Relevant Supreme Court and High Court jurisprudence"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Because ADR legislation and institutional rules can evolve, students should always verify the current statutory provisions and applicable institutional rules."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Practical Case Management"},{"type":"p","text":"For a five-year integrated law program, students should move beyond theory."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn to Manage:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case registration"},{"text":"Filing schedules"},{"text":"Procedural timelines"},{"text":"Party communications"},{"text":"Hearing schedules"},{"text":"Arbitrator/mediator coordination"},{"text":"Document management"},{"text":"Fee tracking"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Procedural orders"},{"text":"Case status reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Build a Mock Case File"},{"type":"p","text":"CASE FILE"},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Notice of Arbitration"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Arbitration Agreement"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Claimant Documents"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Respondent Documents"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Tribunal Appointment"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Procedural Order"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Procedural Calendar"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Hearing Schedule"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Submissions"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Correspondence"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Award / Settlement"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 5 / Final Year — Professional Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"Where applicable, focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International arbitration"},{"text":"Investment arbitration fundamentals"},{"text":"Construction arbitration"},{"text":"Commercial arbitration"},{"text":"Technology disputes"},{"text":"Maritime disputes"},{"text":"Mediation administration"},{"text":"Institutional case management"},{"text":"Digital dispute resolution"},{"text":"Legal operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Objective"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should be able to independently demonstrate:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I can understand an ADR proceeding, organise the case record, track deadlines, coordinate participants, manage documents and support the procedural workflow.”"}]},{"heading":"Core Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"ADR Law"},{"text":"Arbitration, mediation, conciliation"}],[{"text":"Case Management"},{"text":"Filing, scheduling, deadlines"}],[{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Statutes, judgments, rules"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Case files, submissions, correspondence"}],[{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Arbitration clauses, commercial contracts"}],[{"text":"Procedure"},{"text":"Hearings, procedural orders, timelines"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Parties, lawyers, tribunals"}],[{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"E-hearing and document systems"}],[{"text":"Administration"},{"text":"Fees, appointments, logistics"}],[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Secure handling of dispute records"}],[{"text":"Project Management"},{"text":"Multi-party case coordination"}],[{"text":"International ADR"},{"text":"Institutional and cross-border proceedings"}]]}]},{"heading":"ADR Case Management Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Case Intake","Conflict / Administrative Checks","Case Registration","Notify Parties","Appointment of Arbitrator / Mediator","Procedural Calendar","Submissions & Documents","Hearing Coordination","Evidence / Transcripts / Exhibits","Procedural Follow-Up","Award / Settlement","Case Closure","Archive & Reporting"]},{"type":"p","text":"The actual workflow differs between arbitration institutions and mediation centres."}]},{"heading":"Tools & Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Become proficient with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SCC Online"},{"text":"Manupatra"},{"text":"Indian Kanoon"},{"text":"Official legislation sources"},{"text":"Court websites"},{"text":"Arbitration institution rules"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microsoft Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PDF management"},{"text":"Document comparison"},{"text":"Cloud document management"},{"text":"Case-management platforms"},{"text":"Digital filing systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"A case manager should be able to maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case trackers"},{"text":"Hearing schedules"},{"text":"Deadline calendars"},{"text":"Party information"},{"text":"Fee trackers"},{"text":"Arbitrator databases"},{"text":"Case-status dashboards"}]}]},{"heading":"Technology for ADR","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern ADR is increasingly digital."},{"type":"h","text":"Virtual Hearings"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic administration of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Zoom"},{"text":"Microsoft Teams"},{"text":"Webex"},{"text":"Secure video-conferencing systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic documents"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Document indexing"},{"text":"Digital evidence management"},{"text":"Secure file sharing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & LegalTech"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted legal research"},{"text":"Document summarisation"},{"text":"Contract analysis"},{"text":"Chronology generation"},{"text":"Case-document classification"},{"text":"Legal document search"},{"text":"Hearing transcription"},{"text":"Translation tools"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI output should be treated as an assistive tool, with legal documents and procedural communications reviewed by qualified professionals."}]},{"heading":"Projects During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Mock Arbitration Case Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a fictional commercial dispute."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Company A claims that Company B breached a supply agreement."},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case registration form"},{"text":"Arbitration agreement"},{"text":"Party details"},{"text":"Procedural calendar"},{"text":"Hearing schedule"},{"text":"Document index"},{"text":"Communication tracker"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Arbitration Case Timeline"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"table","header":["Event","Date","Responsible Party","Status"],"rows":[[{"text":"Notice of Arbitration"},{"text":"Day 1"},{"text":"Claimant"},{"text":"Completed"}],[{"text":"Response"},{"text":"Day 14"},{"text":"Respondent"},{"text":"Completed"}],[{"text":"Tribunal Appointment"},{"text":"Day 30"},{"text":"Institution"},{"text":"Pending"}],[{"text":"Procedural Conference"},{"text":"Day 45"},{"text":"Tribunal"},{"text":"Scheduled"}],[{"text":"Statement of Claim"},{"text":"Day 60"},{"text":"Claimant"},{"text":"Pending"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates practical case-management ability."}]},{"heading":"Project 3 — Mediation Administration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Create a mock mediation file containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case intake"},{"text":"Party information"},{"text":"Conflict-check documentation"},{"text":"Mediator appointment"},{"text":"Session schedule"},{"text":"Confidentiality documentation"},{"text":"Settlement discussion tracker"},{"text":"Settlement agreement framework"}]}]},{"heading":"Project 4 — Arbitration Rules Comparison","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Compare the procedural structure of selected institutional arbitration rules."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case commencement"},{"text":"Arbitrator appointment"},{"text":"Filing requirements"},{"text":"Timelines"},{"text":"Hearings"},{"text":"Fees"},{"text":"Emergency/interim procedures"},{"text":"Award procedures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly valuable for students interested in international arbitration."}]},{"heading":"Project 5 — ADR Case Dashboard","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Create an Excel or Power BI dashboard showing:"},{"type":"p","text":"Total Cases"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Arbitration"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Mediation"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Conciliation"},{"type":"p","text":"Case Status"},{"type":"p","text":"├── New"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Ongoing"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Hearing"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Award"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Closed"},{"type":"p","text":"Deadlines"},{"type":"p","text":"├── This Week"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Upcoming"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Overdue"},{"type":"p","text":"This adds a useful legal operations + analytics dimension to the profile."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"First Internship"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Litigation law firms"},{"text":"Dispute-resolution practices"},{"text":"Legal aid organisations"},{"text":"Mediation centres"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Case files"},{"text":"Court procedure"},{"text":"Legal drafting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Second Internship"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arbitration practices"},{"text":"Commercial law firms"},{"text":"ADR institutions"},{"text":"Corporate legal departments"}]},{"t